# 3. architecture
c('architecture', 'Browser calls run on Daily WebRTC: the homepage demo POSTed api.vapi.ai/call/web (201) which returned transport.provider "daily" and a vapi.daily.co room; signalling went to wss://ip-129-158-55-187s-iad.wss.daily.co; the SFU is mediasoup (SDP o=mediasoup-client), Opus 48 kHz; the Vapi bot joined as a second participant with countryCode "USA". Confirms l4b demo-inventory (Daily).', 'observed', T + 'demo-call/demo-call-signal.json', T + 'demo-call/demo-call.redacted.har', L + 'l4b-measured/data/demo-inventory.csv')
c('architecture', 'Daily room metadata from the same capture: SFU worker group "oke-us-ashburn-1" (Oracle Kubernetes Engine, US-Ashburn), geoGroup us-east-1, turn_providers "cloudflare,twilio", enable_transcription true, allow_sip and allow_dialout on; the SFU IP 129.158.55.187 is registered to Oracle (RDAP). The relayed path used Twilio TURN over TLS 443 (54.172.60.x, AWS us-east-1).', 'observed', T + 'demo-call/demo-call.redacted.har (gs.daily.co/rooms/check)', T + 'net/rdap-129.158.55.187.json', T + 'net/aws-ip-ranges.json')
c('architecture', 'Call orchestration for the default (US) region runs in AWS us-west-2: the call/web response gave monitor listen/control URLs on phone-call-websocket.aws-us-west-2-backend-production1.vapi.ai, which resolves to 44.249.229.131 (AWS us-west-2 EC2). The hostname printed in the docs (aws-us-west-2-production1-phone-call-websocket.vapi.ai) does not resolve: the docs example is stale.', 'observed', T + 'demo-call/demo-call.redacted.har (api.vapi.ai/call/web response)', T + 'net/aws-ip-ranges.json', T + 'docs-md/calls__call-features.md')
c('architecture', 'API edge: api.vapi.ai and dashboard.vapi.ai sit behind Cloudflare (104.18.24/25.64; cf-ray IAD) and the API answers with x-powered-by: Express (Node). DTO-style schema names (CreateCampaignDTO) suggest a NestJS-style codebase (inference).', 'observed', T + 'demo-call/demo-call.redacted.har', T + 'openapi/api.vapi.ai_api-json')
c('architecture', 'Own SIP SBCs: sip.vapi.ai = 44.229.228.186 / 44.238.177.138 (AWS us-west-2), sip.eu.vapi.ai = 63.182.83.170 (AWS eu-central-1); US RTP media uses dynamic IPs. The status page also shows "Australia SIP Infra" maintenance and the May 2026 RCA names "EU and AUS regions": three regions (US, EU, AUS), none in India.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/advanced__sip__sip-networking.md', T + 'net/aws-ip-ranges.json', T + 'status/s_feed.rss')
c('architecture', 'Static egress range 167.150.224.0/23 is registered to Vapi Inc. (ARIN, 2025-10-21) with an Oracle Cloud BYOIP token in the registration remarks; inference: some Vapi egress (webhooks) runs on Oracle Cloud, so the platform is multi-cloud (AWS + OCI) beyond Daily\'s own OCI SFUs.', 'inferred', T + 'net/rdap-167.150.224.1.json', T + 'docs-md/security-and-privacy__static-ip-addresses.md')
c('architecture', 'Orchestration is Vapi\'s own streaming pipeline, not Pipecat or LiveKit Agents: Vapi\'s engineering posts describe 20 ms audio chunks, a 4-state VAD in a separate process (~200 ms to start, ~800 ms sustained silence to stop), adaptive background-speech filtering, confidence-filtered streaming STT, an endpointing model that "predicts and scraps" LLM requests, and LLM routing across 40+ Azure OpenAI deployments using Redis latency tables and hedged retries. LiveKit appears only as an English smart-endpointing model option.', 'vendor-claimed', T + 'blog/how-we-built-vapi-s-voice-ai-pipeline-part-1.txt', T + 'blog/how-we-built-vapi-s-voice-ai-pipeline-part-2.txt', T + 'blog/how-we-solved-latency-at-vapi.txt', T + 'docs-md/customization__voice-pipeline-configuration.md')
c('architecture', 'No Pipecat or LiveKit agent code appears in what we can see: the web SDK depends only on daily-js and events; the dashboard bundle has 0 LiveKit client strings. This supports (does not prove) own orchestration; the server is closed.', 'inferred', T + 'sdk-npm-web/x/package/package.json', R + 'bundle-findings.json')
c('architecture', 'Platform internals per Vapi (Aug 2025): primary DB moved from Supabase to Neon with an AWS Aurora fallback, a cache serving 80% of eligible reads, SIP moved from one EC2 instance (~200 concurrent calls) to auto-scaling groups, LLM fallback chain OpenAI -> Azure OpenAI -> AWS Bedrock, multi-cluster Kubernetes with a canary manager, Lambda burst workers via a QUIC proxy, Temporal for payments/number purchase/user creation, and "every call runs in its own isolated virtual machine".', 'vendor-claimed', T + 'blog/how-we-achieved-99-99-reliability-at-vapi.txt')
c('architecture', 'Job posts (8 open, all San Francisco) name Kubernetes, Argo CD, Terraform, Atlantis, Envoy, Postgres, Aurora, Redis, Kafka, ClickHouse, TypeScript/Go/Python; a 5-person infrastructure team; a 4-person trust-and-safety team covering billing, fraud and outbound telephony; and "hundreds of pull requests a day". No India-based role.', 'vendor-claimed', T + 'jobs/ashby-vapi.json')
c('architecture', 'Dashboard stack: Vite/React-Router SPA, 561 JS files (17.7 MB) with no source maps referenced and none served (.map 404); auth migrating from Supabase auth helpers to WorkOS (use-workos-auth flag, /auth/workos/* routes); Stripe billing; Cloudflare Turnstile on sign-up; PostHog with session recording and surveys; Sentry; Nango for integration OAuth; daily-js 0.91.0 bundled.', 'observed', R + 'bundle-findings.json', T + 'rea/dashboard-login-inspect-web-page.json', T + 'har/dashboard-login-2026-10-20.redacted.har')
c('architecture', 'The homepage demo widget loads daily-js 0.85.0, which Daily itself flags in the console as "no longer supported", and downloads Krisp noise-cancellation weights (c.daily.co/static/krisp/v2.2.1).', 'observed', T + 'demo-call/demo-call-signal.json (console)', T + 'demo-call/demo-call.redacted.har')
c('architecture', 'Providers are a catalogue, not a stack: 11 transcriber providers (Deepgram, AssemblyAI, Azure, Cartesia, ElevenLabs, Gladia, Google, OpenAI, Soniox, Speechmatics, xAI), 18 LLM providers and 15 voice providers incl. Smallest AI and Vapi Voices (3 "Indian American" accent voices: Naina, Rohan, Sagar). The demo call response did not expose which providers the homepage agent uses (unknown).', 'observed', T + 'docs/docs.vapi.ai_llms.txt', T + 'docs-md/providers__voice__vapi-voices.md', T + 'demo-call/demo-call.redacted.har')
c('architecture', 'Hindi/Hinglish handling is configuration, with English-first defaults: smart endpointing via LiveKit is English-only, non-English uses Vapi\'s own endpointing or transcription heuristics; multilingual STT means Deepgram Nova-2/3 "multi", Deepgram Flux multilingual (2026-04-27), Google or Gladia. No Indian-language quality claim appears in the docs. Consistent with l4b CMP-03 (Gujarati replies to Hinglish).', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/customization__voice-pipeline-configuration.md', T + 'docs-md/customization__multilingual.md', T + 'changelog/entries/2026-4-27.md', L + 'l4b-measured/report.md')
c('architecture', 'REA as a tool: inspect-web-network-capture rejected raw HARs over its 32 MB budget (fixed by slimming bodies), then only normalised records (no stack inference); analyze-web-bundle on the dashboard ran >5 min at ~6 GB RSS with no output before our 300 s timeout; inspect-web-page worked (58 scripts, 0 source maps, storage keys incl. AUTH_PROVIDER). Stack facts came from our own HAR/bundle analysis.', 'observed', T + 'rea/dashboard-login-har-inspect.json', T + 'rea/dashboard-login-analyze-web-bundle.err', T + 'rea/dashboard-login-inspect-web-page.json')

# 4. pricing
c('pricing', 'Pricing page 2026-10-20: $0.05/min hosting (unchanged since 2024-06, 28 months, per pricing-history.json); models "pass-through at cost"; $5 free credits (2024: $10); Usage-only 4 concurrent lines / 2 orgs / 1 Vapi number / 14-day retention / no SLA; Core $29/mo (10 lines, ZDR included); Pro $999/mo minimum or 10% of hosting fees (30 lines, RBAC, 99% SLA); Premier custom (99.9%, SSO, dedicated SIP, EU region); add-ons $10/line/month, $20/org/month, HIPAA $2,000/month. Change vs 2026-06-06 history: ZDR moved from a $1K/mo add-on into every Success Package.', 'observed', T + 'pricing/vapi.ai_pricing.html', L + 'l4a-competitors/pricing-history.json')
c('pricing', 'The dashboard code still carries an older bundled-plan table: Agency $500/mo with 3,000 minutes ($0.18 overage, 50 lines), Startup $1,000 / 7,500 min ($0.16, 100 lines), Growth $5,000 / 40,000 min ($0.14, 500 lines), Scale $10,000 / 100,000 min ($0.12, 1,000 lines, not public). Undated; not on today\'s pricing page.', 'observed', R + 'bundle-findings.json (legacy_bundled_plans_snippet)')
c('pricing', 'All-in buyer price for an Indian outbound minute on Vapi via Twilio (the only documented route; Twilio allows outbound to India only from non-Indian numbers at $0.0496/min to Indian mobiles): USD 0.131-0.179/min = INR 12.5-17.0/min at FX 95, of which INR 9.46 is hosting plus telephony before any AI. Confirms ECO-17 (INR 11.6-17.5 at FX 88).', 'inferred', R + 'pricing.json', T + 'pricing/twilio_voice_pricing_in.html', T + 'india/www.twilio.com_en-us_guidelines_in_voice', 'research/2026-10-17/ledger.md (ECO-17)')
c('pricing', 'Reconstructed Vapi-side COGS: model and telephony lines are pass-through (0 margin unless platform-key discounts exist, unknown); the $0.05 hosting fee carries an estimated USD 0.001-0.005/min of own cost (per-call VM, SBC, media relay, storage, DB, logs), i.e. an estimated 90-98% gross margin on hosting. Not measured.', 'inferred', R + 'pricing.json', T + 'blog/how-we-achieved-99-99-reliability-at-vapi.txt', 'https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46189900')
c('pricing', 'Concurrency is a paid gate for campaigns: 4 lines on Usage-only; a 30-line Indian operation needs Pro ($999/mo) or Core + 20 add-on lines ($229/mo); concurrency is shared across all inbound, outbound and campaign calls in the subscription, and docs advise chunking lists into batches of 50-100 numbers.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/billing__pricing-and-success-packages.md', T + 'docs-md/calls__call-concurrency.md')

