# 6. India plumbing
c('india-plumbing', 'Vapi cannot terminate Indian numbers: its Plivo SIP guide says "Indian phone numbers cannot be used with Plivo on Vapi due to TRAI regulations. These regulations require SIP termination to occur via an Indian server, which Vapi does not currently support." Plivo\'s own Vapi guide repeats it.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/advanced__sip__plivo.md', T + 'india/plivo.com_docs_voice-agents_sip-trunking_integration-guides_vapi')
c('india-plumbing', 'The only documented outbound route to Indian handsets is international: Twilio\'s India guideline says "Outbound calls to India can only be made from international (non-Indian) numbers" and warns that high volumes of short calls may trigger carrier blocks. An Indian enterprise on Vapi therefore cannot present a 140xx, 1600xx or declared 10-digit Indian CLI.', 'observed', T + 'india/www.twilio.com_en-us_guidelines_in_voice', T + 'docs-md/advanced__sip__plivo.md')
c('india-plumbing', 'Consequence (inference from the two observations above and the regulation lane): Vapi cannot be used as-is for regulated Indian calling. BFSI service calls must come from 1600xx and promotional calls from 140xx (RS-07); every AI call is A2P and must be declared on DLT (RS-08). Vapi offers none of the series, DLT registration or A2P declaration, so an Indian buyer must bridge through an Indian-licensed provider by WebSocket or middleware.', 'inferred', T + 'docs-md/advanced__sip__plivo.md', 'research/2026-10-20/teardown/regulation-segment/claims.json (RS-07, RS-08)', T + 'india/dev.to_animesh_gupta_705a19fc6f8_how-to-give-your-livekit-vapi-or-retell-voice-agent-a-real-indian-91-phone-number-am6')
c('india-plumbing', 'Compliance features are US-shaped and left to the buyer: a TCPA consent guide, recording-consent plans (stay-on-line or verbal), HIPAA ($2K/mo), PCI, ZDR, SOC 2, GDPR; calling-window advice says "choose a window that complies with the consent, quiet-hours, and telemarketing rules"; the docs index has 0 hits for DND, NCPR, DLT, TRAI (outside the Plivo warning) or DPDP. Terms make the customer solely responsible (RS-24). Confirms l4a parity compliance_dnd_dlt_consent = partial.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/tcpa-consent.md', T + 'docs-md/security-and-privacy__recording-consent-plan.md', T + 'docs/docs.vapi.ai_llms.txt', 'research/2026-10-20/teardown/regulation-segment/claims.json (RS-24)', L + 'l4a-competitors/parity.csv')
c('india-plumbing', 'Calling windows are one absolute range per campaign: schedulePlan {earliestAt, latestAt}, at most 7 days ahead in 15-minute steps, one time zone per campaign ("A campaign uses one time zone and calling window for every contact"); there is no recurring daily window, no per-contact time zone and no retry policy. Contacts not dispatched by latestAt are dropped; the only retry is up to 1 hour waiting for concurrency.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/outbound-campaigns__scheduling-and-lifecycle.md', T + 'openapi/api.vapi.ai_api-json (SchedulePlan)', R + 'bundle-findings.json (campaign_wizard_strings)')
c('india-plumbing', 'Retries, attempt budgets and suppression are explicitly the buyer\'s job: "The organization running the campaigns owns the approved contacts, the recurring schedule, the daily attempt budgets, the retry rules, and the review process. Vapi places the calls." The pre-dial webhook is the only hook for consent or suppression checks.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/outbound-campaigns__number-warming.md', T + 'docs-md/outbound-campaigns__webhooks.md')
c('india-plumbing', 'Data residency: regions are US (default), EU (Premier only) and AUS; there is no India region. Model-level Azure region pinning exists for GPT-5 (e.g. gpt-5:eastus2), and the model picker lists Azure OpenAI deployments with an ":india" suffix, but audio, transcripts and recordings stay in the org\'s region. Confirms l4a on_prem_india_residency = partial.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/security-and-privacy__eu-region.md', T + 'changelog/entries/2026-8-17.md', R + 'bundle-findings.json', T + 'status/s_feed.rss')
c('india-plumbing', 'Dashboard CSV hygiene is minimal and India-hostile: the phone normaliser strips spaces, dashes, brackets and quotes and prepends "+" when missing (function os), so a 10-digit Indian mobile "98xxxxxxxx" becomes "+98xxxxxxxx" (Iran country code) and "0xxxxxxxxxx" becomes "+0..."; a row fails only if the number is missing or empty. One failing row rejects the whole upload ("Phone number validation errors. Please update the CSV and upload again."). There is no duplicate detection and no opt-out column.', 'observed', R + 'bundle-findings.json (campaign_csv_phone_normaliser, campaign_csv_row_validation, campaign_csv_reject_on_error)', T + 'dashboard-js-lazy/js__index-Dy8CkNeM.js')
c('india-plumbing', 'An Indian (+91) number appears in Vapi\'s own call-concurrency docs example, and Vapi Voices include 3 "Indian American" accent voices: India is present as usage, not as a supported market.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/calls__call-concurrency.md', T + 'docs-md/providers__voice__vapi-voices.md')

# 7. failure modes
c('failure-modes', 'Trustpilot 2026-10-20: TrustScore 2.5/5 on 16 reviews; 1-2 star themes: support (2025-12-11 "expect to be waiting a week"; 2025-07-01 help bot), billing (2025-12-09 "Hidden charges"; 2026-04-01 HIPAA "$1000"), latency (2026-03-25 "the latency of the models is bad"; 2026-03-28 "lags a lot"), DTMF (2025-05-06), telephony (2024-10-08 "no support for UK to buy numbers"), account deletion (2024-07-29). Extends the 10 Vapi Trustpilot rows in l4a complaints.csv; those rows carry earlier (likely date-of-experience) dates.', 'observed', T + 'complaints/trustpilot-webfetch-2026-10-20.txt', 'https://www.trustpilot.com/review/vapi.ai', L + 'l4a-competitors/complaints.csv')
c('failure-modes', 'LATENCY, dashboard vs reality: forum threads report "system latency shows around 575-1000ms, the actual response time during live calls is 3-4 seconds, and sometimes it goes up to 6-7 seconds" and "Actual latency is 4x of the estimated latency"; our 2026-10-17 measurement of the homepage demo gave clean-turn p50 2.32 s (n=40) against Vapi\'s own stated 1,200 ms turn budget.', 'observed', 'https://support.vapi.ai/t/23432400/is-someone-else-observing-issues-with-latency-and-the-ai-get', 'https://support.vapi.ai/t/27105720/actual-latency-is-4x-of-the-estimated-latency', L + 'l4b-measured/report.md', T + 'blog/how-we-solved-latency-at-vapi.txt')
c('failure-modes', 'BILLING: an HN user reported "60-70% of our total spend was the Vapi platform fee, and only 30-40% was actual LLM/STT/TTS usage"; a forum thread is titled "assistant hallucinating and vapi overcharging". Structural cause (inference): a fixed $0.05/min platform fee on top of pass-through model costs.', 'observed', 'https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46189900', 'https://support.vapi.ai/t/26876220/assistant-hallucinating-and-vapi-overcharging', R + 'pricing.json')
c('failure-modes', 'RELIABILITY vs claims: Vapi\'s Aug 2025 blog claims 99.99% uptime and "<5 second failover"; its own May 2026 RCA records ~4 h 07 min of total US outage because "two databases that every call and API request depends on" failed together (the replica shared the provider\'s project-level config), and "Scheduled and campaign calls due to fire during the window did not run and were not retried automatically." A Trustpilot reviewer claimed "$50k in damages so far from downtime" (2025-12-11, l4a row).', 'observed', T + 'status/s_feed.rss (RCA 2026-05-29)', T + 'blog/how-we-achieved-99-99-reliability-at-vapi.txt', L + 'l4a-competitors/complaints.csv')
c('failure-modes', 'Inference: the database provider in the May 2026 outage was Neon. Vapi names Neon as its primary DB (blog), and the RCA uses Neon-style terms ("project-wide" setting, "apply_config", "database endpoint" restart, "pod"). Not confirmed by Vapi.', 'inferred', T + 'blog/how-we-achieved-99-99-reliability-at-vapi.txt', T + 'status/s_feed.rss')
c('failure-modes', 'SUPPORT is tiered by price: Usage-only gets Discord peer help and "email support without a response service-level agreement"; a 2-business-day SLA starts at Core and 1-hour P0 only at Premier. The support forum (support.vapi.ai) sits behind a Vercel security checkpoint and answered our fetches 429; we did not work around it.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/billing__pricing-and-success-packages.md', T + 'complaints/trustpilot-webfetch-2026-10-20.txt')
c('failure-modes', 'TELEPHONY/IVR: Trustpilot "did not work in testing like dtmf tones" (2025-05-06); Retell community thread "Getting blocked by vapi for testing a simple IVR agent" (2026-07-04, l4a row); Vapi\'s blog claims 98%+ DTMF success via a native-API-then-audio fallback (vendor-claimed). For India, a support thread asks whether a US Twilio number suffices for Indian outbound.', 'observed', 'https://www.trustpilot.com/review/vapi.ai', 'https://community.retellai.com/t/3258', T + 'blog/how-we-achieved-99-99-reliability-at-vapi.txt', 'https://support.vapi.ai/t/33237506/indian-number-outbound-calling-us-twilio-number-sufficient')
c('failure-modes', 'ACCOUNT_UI: "Your draft agent doesn\'t hold the prompt" (Trustpilot, l4a row) and "I don\'t like Vapi due to 1) extensive GUI driven experience, 2) cost" (HN 46385230). Vapi\'s 2026 answer is Composer, a new publish flow (flag enable-new-publish-flow) and GitOps config-as-code.', 'observed', L + 'l4a-competitors/complaints.csv', 'https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46385230', R + 'bundle-findings.json (feature_flags)', T + 'docs-md/config-as-code.md')
c('failure-modes', 'Blocked sources (not bypassed): Reddit JSON 403, G2 403, support.vapi.ai Vercel checkpoint/429, GitHub issues API and github.com (session-scoped proxy 403). The complaint sample is Trustpilot + HN + forum titles via search + the status page, so it is small and skewed to small developers.', 'observed', T + 'complaints/', 'https://api.github.com/repos/VapiAI/client-sdk-web/issues (403 in this session)')

# 8. v2
c('v2', 'Memory across calls: none in the docs (0 hits for "memory" in the 307-page index). Personalisation is server-supplied at call time (assistant-request webhook or dynamic variables from CSV columns, max 100,000 chars per contact). Confirms the l4a parity row memory_across_calls = unknown as a bounded negative.', 'observed', T + 'docs/docs.vapi.ai_llms.txt', T + 'docs-md/assistants__personalization.md', T + 'docs-md/outbound-campaigns__contact-data.md', L + 'l4a-competitors/parity.csv')
c('v2', 'The learning loop is tooling plus human: Monitoring (monitors, scheduled triggers on Insights, issues, notifiers; GA 2026-04-13), Scorecards, Structured outputs, Evals (text decisions), Simulations (AI-tester voice/chat suites), Traffic splitting (manual percentage canaries, no statistics, per LRN-09) and a flag-gated Composer "Improve the assistant" kickoff. Nothing applies changes automatically; Composer "cannot deploy to production automatically".', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/observability__monitoring-quickstart.md', T + 'docs-md/composer.md', T + 'docs-md/assistants__versioning__traffic-splitting.md', R + 'bundle-findings.json', 'research/2026-10-17/ledger.md (LRN-09)')
c('v2', 'Marketing vs docs: the homepage promises to "continuously improve the experiences that drive your business forward" and "Build, deploy, and improve voice agents as fast as you ship"; the docs implement improvement as manual monitor -> issue -> human fix -> regression test. This is a milder version of the CMP-01 marketing/docs gap; Vapi makes no memory claim.', 'observed', T + 'docs/vapi.ai_index', T + 'docs-md/observability__monitoring-quickstart.md', 'research/2026-10-17/ledger.md (CMP-01)')
c('v2', 'GPT-Live (beta): an OpenAI full-duplex speech model as the "speaker" plus a separate "reasoner" model for tools, with no separate STT/TTS. The flags enable-full-duplex-harness and enable-multi-harness suggest Vapi is building more than one orchestration harness.', 'observed', T + 'docs-md/gpt-live__overview.md', R + 'bundle-findings.json (feature_flags)')

